  ('auth-recovery-audit-3', 'Kiểm kê khôi phục tài khoản', '3. CHI TIẾT CÁC CƠ CHẾ SAI LỆCH VÀ BẢN VÁ CẦN LOẠI BỎ', '## 3. CHI TIẾT CÁC CƠ CHẾ SAI LỆCH VÀ BẢN VÁ CẦN LOẠI BỎ

| Cơ chế bị lỗi / Nguy hiểm | Vị trí định nghĩa | Rủi ro / Nguyên nhân lỗi | Biện pháp sửa chữa |
|---|---|---|---|
| Bảng `private.password_reset_requests` | `20260930002100_...sql` | Chứa cột `new_password TEXT` lưu mật khẩu thô. | Xóa bảng / Drop table, xóa sạch dữ liệu nhạy cảm. |
| Hàm `private.reset_password_direct` | `20260930001900_...sql` | Ghi trực tiếp vào `auth.users.encrypted_password`. | Thu hồi quyền, Drop function. Dùng Supabase Admin API. |
| Hàm `private.process_password_reset` | `20260930002100_...sql` | Quét bảng và ghi trực tiếp `encrypted_password`. | Drop function. |
| Hàm `private.sync_auth_email` | `20260930001700_...sql` | Ghi trực tiếp `auth.users.email = username || ''@internal...''`. | Drop function. Không dùng SQL sửa auth email. |
| Trigger `private.new_auth_user` | `20260930001700_...sql` | Cố ý tự động cập nhật `auth.users.email` trong trigger. | Viết lại trigger: Chỉ khởi tạo `public.profiles`, tuyệt đối không mutate `auth.users`. |
| Policy `profiles_update` trên `profiles` | `20260930001000_...sql` | Cho phép `authenticated` UPDATE profile mà không kiểm tra trường nhạy cảm (`role`, `active`). | Thu hồi `GRANT UPDATE, DELETE`, xóa policy sai, trả lại nguyên tắc: Mọi cập nhật profile qua RPC `update_profile` hoặc Edge Function OWNER. |
| Policy `profiles_delete` trên `profiles` | `20260930001000_...sql` | `GRANT DELETE` cho `authenticated`. | Thu hồi quyền DELETE từ client. |
| Hard delete trong Edge Function `manage-users` | `manage-users/index.ts` | Gọi `admin.auth.admin.deleteUser` khi còn ràng buộc RESTRICT tại `profiles`. | Kiểm tra ràng buộc kinh doanh trước khi hard delete tài khoản chưa dùng; ưu tiên Soft Deactivate. |
| Ép email ảo tại `LoginPage.tsx` | `LoginPage.tsx` | `username` được ghép cứng `@internal.xecrm.app` bất kể có `@` hay không. | Hỗ trợ đăng nhập kép: Nếu có `@` -> Email thật; Nếu không có `@` -> Resolve hoặc dùng alias nội bộ. |

---', 'OWNER', 'docs/AUTH_RECOVERY_AUDIT.md'),
  ('auth-recovery-audit-4', 'Kiểm kê khôi phục tài khoản', '4. KẾ HOẠCH HÀNH ĐỘNG PHỤC HỒI (RECOVERY ROADMAP)', '## 4. KẾ HOẠCH HÀNH ĐỘNG PHỤC HỒI (RECOVERY ROADMAP)

1. **Bảo vệ và phục hồi tài khoản OWNER**:
   - Sử dụng Admin API / Forward migration để khôi phục `auth.users.email` của OWNER về `macxuanhoa211002@gmail.com`, đồng bộ với `auth.identities`.
   - Giữ nguyên `profile.username = ''macxuanhoa21100211''` (hoặc rút gọn nếu hợp lệ) nhưng tách rời khỏi Auth email.
   - Đảm bảo tài khoản OWNER luôn có `active = true`, không bị khóa bởi lịch trình hay giờ giấc.

2. **Dọn dẹp bảng và hàm độc hại**:
   - Tạo migration mới `20260930002200_auth_recovery_and_account_control.sql` (Forward-only, tuyệt đối không sửa migration cũ).
   - Xóa bảng `private.password_reset_requests` và hủy các hàm SQL can thiệp `auth.users`.
   - Siết chặt RLS trên `public.profiles`: Thu hồi `UPDATE`, `DELETE` trực tiếp từ phía client.

3. **Củng cố kiểm soát lịch truy cập và Múi giờ**:
   - Chuẩn hóa múi giờ kinh doanh: `Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh`.
   - Cập nhật hàm `private.is_active()` và `private.current_role()` để kiểm tra trạng thái hoạt động thực tế (`active`, `disabled_until`, `allowed_from`, `allowed_until`, `working_days`, `deleted_at`).
   - Miễn trừ tường minh vai trò `OWNER` khỏi các giới hạn giờ giấc làm việc của nhân viên.

4. **Tái cấu trúc Edge Function `manage-users`**:
   - Chỉ cho phép OWNER thao tác.
   - Tạo người dùng: Atomic & Rollback an toàn (nếu tạo profile thất bại thì rollback Auth user).
   - Đặt lại mật khẩu: Sử dụng `admin.auth.admin.updateUserById(userId, { password })` và đánh dấu `must_change_password = true`.
   - Xóa người dùng: Mặc định Deactivate (`active = false`, `deleted_at = now()`). Chỉ cho phép Hard Delete nếu tài khoản **hoàn toàn chưa từng phát sinh dữ liệu nghiệp vụ** (kiểm tra `acquisitions`, `vehicles`, `sales`, `payments`, `expenses`, `audit_logs`).

5. **Cải tiến UI & AuthProvider**:
   - `LoginPage.tsx`: Nhập email (chứa `@`) hoặc username (không chứa `@`).
   - `AuthProvider.tsx`: Luồng xác thực gọn gàng, tính toán múi giờ Việt Nam, xử lý thông báo tiếng Việt thân thiện khi tài khoản bị khóa/hết giờ làm việc.
   - `UsersPage.tsx`: Loại bỏ các nút vá lỗi (như nút "Đồng bộ email"), hoàn thiện giao diện quản lý phân quyền, lịch làm việc, đổi mật khẩu tạm.', 'OWNER', 'docs/AUTH_RECOVERY_AUDIT.md'),
  ('api-preamble', 'Hợp đồng database và RPC', null, '# Database contract

All operations require a verified Supabase session and an active profile. Functions are atomic PostgreSQL transactions. Table writes are denied to browser roles. Financial columns live in separate RLS-protected tables; the JSON functions omit sensitive keys unless the caller is OWNER or MANAGER with `can_view_financials`.

| RPC | Arguments | Result |
| --- | --- | --- |
| list_vehicles | p_filters jsonb = {} | {items,total} |
| get_vehicle | p_id uuid | Vehicle with images, expenses, sales, activity |
| save_vehicle | p_data jsonb, p_id uuid = null | UUID |
| sell_vehicle | p_data jsonb | sale UUID |
| cancel_sale | p_id uuid, p_reason text | void |
| add_payment | p_data jsonb | payment UUID |
| list_sales | p_filters jsonb = {} | {items,total} |
| get_sale | p_id uuid | Sale with vehicle, payments, paid_amount, remaining_amount |
| list_expenses | p_filters jsonb = {} | {items,total} |
| save_expense | p_kind text, p_data jsonb, p_id uuid = null | UUID |
| cancel_expense | p_kind text, p_id uuid, p_reason text | void |
| dashboard | p_from date = first day of month, p_to date = today | Metrics and lists |
| report | p_kind text, p_filters jsonb = {} | {items,total} |
| list_audit | p_filters jsonb = {} | {items,total} |
| list_profiles | none | Profile[] |
| update_profile | p_id uuid, p_data jsonb | void |
| get_settings | none | settings object |
| save_settings | p_data jsonb | void |
| register_vehicle_image | p_vehicle_id uuid, p_storage_path text, p_display_order int = 0 | UUID |
| remove_vehicle_image | p_id uuid | void |
| search_knowledge | p_query text, p_limit int = 8 (max 20) | Ranked sections: slug,title,section,audience,source_path,rank,excerpt |
| list_knowledge | none | {items:[slug,title,section,audience,source_path],total} |
| get_knowledge_article | p_slug text | Article with body_md,audience,source_path,updated_at |

List filters: `offset` (default 0), `limit` (default 25; max 100), `search`. Vehicle filters: `status` (enum value, `ALL`, or `AVAILABLE`/`UNSOLD` for IN_STOCK and RESERVED), `brand`, `year`, `min_price`, `max_price`, `date_from`, `date_to`, `sort` (`newest`, `oldest`, `highest_cost`, `highest_price`, `longest_stock`). Sales/expense/report dates: `from`, `to` (also accept `date_from`, `date_to`). Expense kind: `vehicle` or `business` (default both), with optional `vehicle_id`. Report kind: `sales`, `inventory`, `profit`, `vehicle_expenses`, `business_expenses`.

Dashboard period totals, daily sales, top profits, recent sales and recent expenses obey the selected inclusive date range. Today/month counters use the Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh business date. Inventory is current stock; `inventory_cost_pending` counts missing costs and `inventory_indicator` is LOW/NORMAL/HIGH using saved low/high stock thresholds. Inventory reports filter current stock by intake date; they are not historical stock reconstructions.

Vehicle purchase cost is optional only for operational users. Missing cost is stored as NULL, exposed as `cost_pending:true`, and blocks selling until an authorized financial user enters the actual purchase cost. `purchase_price` and `total_cost` keys are absent for unauthorized users. Expense lists require OWNER or MANAGER. Staff can add/update operational vehicle information and sell vehicles with completed costs.

Sale creation data: `vehicle_id,customer_name,customer_phone,sale_price,sale_date,initial_payment,payment_method,notes`. Payment data: `sale_id,amount,payment_method,payment_date,reference,notes`. Required VND amounts are exact nonnegative integers, single-entry cap 1,000,000,000,000. Payment amounts must be positive, and total payments may not exceed the sale price. Payments remain immutable; cancelling a sale excludes its retained payments from active collection totals and marks them `VOIDED`, preserving their history. Actual bank/cash refunds are handled outside this V1 app and must be reconciled separately.

Vehicle images use the private `vehicle-images` bucket, JPEG/PNG/WebP/AVIF only, max 8 MiB. Path is `<vehicle UUID>/<random UUID>.<extension>`. Register metadata after successful upload, then generate short-lived signed URLs. Removing metadata soft-deletes it and removes read access through the storage policy. Objects are retained for audit/backup and can be pruned administratively after the retention period.', 'MANAGER', 'supabase/API.md'),
  ('api-1', 'Hợp đồng database và RPC', 'Knowledge base and AI copilot', '## Knowledge base and AI copilot

`public.knowledge_base` stores one row per documentation section (`slug` unique, `title`, `section`, `body_md`, `audience` in `ALL`/`STAFF`/`MANAGER`/`OWNER`, `source_path`, generated `tsvector` with a GIN index). Browser roles have `SELECT` only, guarded by the `knowledge_base_read` policy and re-checked inside each `SECURITY DEFINER` function through `private.knowledge_visible(audience)`: OWNER reads every tier, MANAGER reads `ALL`/`STAFF`/`MANAGER`, STAFF reads `ALL`/`STAFF`, and disabled or unauthorized callers are rejected by `private.require_role`. Unknown and unauthorized slugs are indistinguishable (`KNOWLEDGE_NOT_FOUND`).

The corpus is generated from repository documentation by `npm run knowledge:seed` (`scripts/build-knowledge-seed.mjs`), which writes `supabase/migrations/20261001002900_knowledge_seed.sql` as an idempotent upsert plus a prune of stale slugs; edit the Markdown files, never the seed migration. The `ai-assist` copilot reads this corpus through `search_knowledge` together with the existing read RPCs and returns a citation for every figure; see [docs/AI_ASSIST_CONTRACT.md](../docs/AI_ASSIST_CONTRACT.md).

`manage-users` Edge Function accepts POST `{email,password,full_name,role,can_view_financials}` for an OWNER to create a user. Role/status updates use `update_profile` RPC; self-profile updates accept only full_name. The final active OWNER cannot be disabled/demoted. Owner provisioning for the first account is documented separately and requires a trusted SQL session.', 'MANAGER', 'supabase/API.md'),
  ('security-preamble', 'Mô hình bảo mật Supabase', null, '# Security and deployment notes', 'OWNER', 'supabase/SECURITY.md'),
  ('security-1', 'Mô hình bảo mật Supabase', 'Database boundaries', '## Database boundaries

- Every application table has RLS enabled. The browser has SELECT only; no INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, or sequence privileges. All mutations pass through explicit functions with active-role checks and an empty `search_path`.
- `vehicle_financials` and `sale_financials` isolate purchase costs and profit from general inventory/sale records. OWNER and financially authorized MANAGER have SELECT through RLS. JSON functions apply the same financial gate. STAFF and nonfinancial MANAGER cannot sort by cost or invoke profit reports.
- Profile defaults are active STAFF (the lowest operational role). Auth `user_metadata` is never trusted for permissions. Public registration is disabled in both local config and production Auth settings. A disabled profile is rejected by every RPC and RLS data policy; profile self-read is the only exception, so the app can explain that access is disabled.
- `private` is not an API-exposed schema. Only small RLS predicates can be executed by authenticated clients. Audit insertion, JSON serialization, money parsing, and role validation helpers are not executable directly.
- `knowledge_base` holds documentation text, never business rows. Audience tiers (`ALL`/`STAFF`/`MANAGER`/`OWNER`) are enforced by an RLS read policy and repeated inside each definer read RPC (`search_knowledge`, `list_knowledge`, `get_knowledge_article`), because `SECURITY DEFINER` bypasses RLS. The corpus comes from tracked markdown via `scripts/build-knowledge-seed.mjs`, so a secret or credential must never be pasted into a documentation file, especially a low-tier one. No browser write access exists.
- `audit_logs`, `vehicle_activity`, and `sale_financials` reject modification/deletion even from privileged SQL unless their protecting triggers are deliberately removed. Authenticated clients cannot append arbitrary audit events. Owner audit contains financial data; the separate operational timeline contains only action, actor, entity, and timestamp.
- Currency is integer VND. The database validates input strings before conversion (no fractional rounding). A single entry is bounded at 1 trillion VND, and aggregates reject values outside JavaScript''s exact integer range.', 'OWNER', 'supabase/SECURITY.md'),
  ('security-2', 'Mô hình bảo mật Supabase', 'Atomicity and cancellation', '## Atomicity and cancellation

All writes affecting a vehicle''s cost or sale state lock the same vehicle row first. `sell_vehicle` locks it, validates availability, captures immutable cost snapshots, inserts the sale/payment, changes the vehicle state, and adds audit events in a single transaction. A partial unique index independently prevents two completed sales for one vehicle. Payment creation and cancellation lock the same vehicle and then sale row, serializing balance checks without deadlock-prone inverse lock ordering.

Expenses and purchase cost cannot change while a vehicle is sold. A sale can be cancelled by OWNER/MANAGER with a recorded reason, returning the vehicle to stock. Payments remain in history as VOIDED and are excluded from active paid balances; they are never deleted. This records business cancellation only. Real refunds must be completed and reconciled separately. A subsequent resale creates a new snapshot and retains the cancelled sale''s original snapshot.

An incomplete purchase cost is NULL, never assumed zero. Operational staff can receive a vehicle without knowing its cost. A financially authorized user must complete the purchase cost before any sale. Inventory value is NULL while any stock vehicle has an unknown cost; `inventory_cost_pending` identifies the count.', 'OWNER', 'supabase/SECURITY.md'),
  ('security-3', 'Mô hình bảo mật Supabase', 'Owner provisioning', '## Owner provisioning

1. Apply migrations to the correct Supabase project.
2. In Supabase Auth, create the initial owner using a verified email and a unique strong password. The trigger creates an inactive profile.
3. In a trusted SQL editor, substitute the actual Auth UUID and run:

```sql
update public.profiles
set full_name = ''Chủ cửa hàng'', role = ''OWNER'', active = true,
    can_view_financials = true, updated_at = now()
where id = ''AUTH-USER-UUID-HERE''::uuid;
```

4. Confirm exactly one expected profile was updated. Sign in and create subsequent users from Users. Never share the owner account. The owner account can be renamed later.
5. Disable public signup in the hosted project''s Auth settings too; `config.toml` configures local services and is not proof that hosted settings changed.

The Edge Function requires `SUPABASE_URL`, a public API key, a server secret API key, and `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` (comma-separated exact origins, e.g. `https://your-store.example`). The handler enforces this list on CORS: a browser `Origin` not in `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` receives no `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` header and the browser blocks the response. Leaving `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` unset falls back to the Supabase SDK default CORS headers and is acceptable only for local development; production deployments must always set it. Legacy environments provide the keys as `SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` and `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`; modern names are listed below. Deploy `manage-users` with JWT verification enabled. The handler also validates the JWT via Auth `getUser`, checks an active OWNER in the database, bounds input, creates an inert account through the server-only Auth Admin API, then activates it through the caller-authorized RPC. If activation fails, the account remains inactive and is returned as `USER_CREATED_INACTIVE`; inspect it in Users instead of retrying blindly. Passwords and tokens are never logged.

Modern key configuration is also supported: `SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY` / `SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY`, or the platform''s named `SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEYS` / `SUPABASE_SECRET_KEYS` JSON objects (preferring `default`). The legacy names above are fallbacks. The browser sends its session JWT as `Authorization: Bearer ...` and its public key as `apikey`; a publishable key by itself never passes the handler''s Auth user verification. See [Edge authorization headers](https://supabase.com/docs/guides/functions/auth-headers) and [API keys](https://supabase.com/docs/guides/getting-started/api-keys). No additional browser admin grants are needed: Auth Admin creation uses the server secret, while profile activation uses the owner''s authenticated RPC permissions.', 'OWNER', 'supabase/SECURITY.md'),
  ('security-4', 'Mô hình bảo mật Supabase', 'AI copilot', '## AI copilot

The `ai-assist` function answers shop questions (`task: ''copilot''`) with a read-only evidence engine. It holds no service-role credential: every figure and document section is fetched with the caller''s own JWT through the existing read RPCs and the knowledge search, so the assistant cannot widen what a STAFF account may already see. Financial keys simply disappear from the payload rather than rendering as zero. Retrieval is deterministic by default and needs no provider configuration. OWNER may request an `llm` summary, which is constrained to re-word the evidence already retrieved for that request; `copilotSchema` and `validateGroundedAnswer` discard any answer citing an unknown evidence id, stating an ungrounded figure or linking outside the app, and the handler falls back to the deterministic answer with a warning. The provider receives no credentials and no raw rows beyond those facts, and images/documents are never sent for copilot. There is no write, draft-application or command endpoint in this path.', 'OWNER', 'supabase/SECURITY.md'),
  ('security-5', 'Mô hình bảo mật Supabase', 'Storage', '## Storage

The `vehicle-images` bucket is private, permits JPEG/PNG/WebP/AVIF, and caps each object at 8 MiB. Object paths must belong to an existing vehicle. No object can be overwritten by a browser. Unregistered objects are not readable. Soft-deleted metadata denies new read requests; already issued signed URLs remain usable until their short expiration. Avoid long-lived signed URLs. Metadata removal retains the physical object for retention/backup. Review abandoned upload objects periodically with a trusted administrator; do not enable broad public policies to make images render.', 'OWNER', 'supabase/SECURITY.md'),
  ('security-6', 'Mô hình bảo mật Supabase', 'Production checklist', '## Production checklist

- Deploy the migrations, Edge Function, and static web build; set HTTPS Auth site URL and exact reset-password redirect URL.
- Supply only the public Supabase URL and anon/publishable key to Vite. Server secrets never use a `VITE_` variable.
- Keep API exposed schemas to public (and Supabase defaults if required); never expose private.
- Re-run authorization tests after modifying any grant, policy, or SECURITY DEFINER function. Do not grant browser table write access.
- Set database backups for the chosen Supabase plan; maintain encrypted external dumps and a separate storage-object backup. A database dump does not contain Storage object bytes or replace Auth configuration backup.
- Restore in an isolated project first; verify owner access, record counts, snapshots, payments, RLS, and image access before changing production endpoints.

Supabase references: [Database functions](https://supabase.com/docs/guides/database/functions), [Row Level Security](https://supabase.com/docs/guides/database/postgres/row-level-security), [Storage access control](https://supabase.com/docs/guides/storage/security/access-control), [Auth getUser](https://supabase.com/docs/reference/javascript/auth-getuser).', 'OWNER', 'supabase/SECURITY.md')
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO UPDATE
SET title = EXCLUDED.title,
    section = EXCLUDED.section,
    body_md = EXCLUDED.body_md,
    audience = EXCLUDED.audience,
    source_path = EXCLUDED.source_path,
    updated_at = now();

-- Drop sections that no longer exist in the tracked documents.
DELETE FROM public.knowledge_base
WHERE source_path IN ('README.md', 'docs/PROJECT_STATE.md', 'docs/OPERATIONS.md', 'docs/DECISIONS.md', 'docs/KNOWN_ISSUES.md', 'docs/VERIFICATION.md', 'docs/COMMUNICATION_ARCHITECTURE.md', 'docs/AI_ASSIST_CONTRACT.md', 'docs/UX_FRICTION_AUDIT.md', 'docs/PRODUCTION_RELEASE.md', 'docs/AGENT_HANDOFF.md', 'docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md', 'docs/IMPLEMENTATION_REPORT.md', 'docs/AUTH_ACCEPTANCE_REPORT.md', 'docs/AUTH_BACKUP_METADATA.md', 'docs/AUTH_RECOVERY_AUDIT.md', 'supabase/API.md', 'supabase/SECURITY.md')
